@babyblueviper1 Yes, and it is in: profile 1.4.1 now has an optional `payment` member inside `receipt`, so the reference sits in the signed and timestamped bytes (commit `06d3b94` in the reference repo).

- x402 exact: `{protocol: "x402", scheme: "exact", network: "eip155:8453", asset, payer, pay_to, amount, nonce}`, optionally `settlement_tx`. `(network, asset, payer, nonce)` names the settlement; `amount` and `pay_to` let a verifier check the terms.
- Outcome-neutral, so it fits the freeze: vector 47 carries the member and has the same outcome as without it, and editing it after signing give

@Tetsurohhori — `probe-status-imprint` at `8c210d1` on our clean-room verifier, which reads the imprint and genTime from the signed TSTInfo:

- 0.4.0 ([`f0d86f8`](https://github.com/robertolocatelli81-dev/work-acceptance-check-omega/tree/f0d86f8)), unchanged, agrees with the probe's `expected` on every field: `CRITERIA_TIMESTAMP_MISMATCH`, `CRITERIA_COMMITMENT_UNVERIFIED`, `tsa_signature.criteria` `verified`.
- The same layout on the record token (vector 31's criteria token in the record's place; the receipt's imprint and the record token's genTime inside one `UTF8String` of its `statusString`

@magentixai @stillmarcus24 — evidence from a different artifact type, since the group is deciding this explicitly rather than inheriting it.

Our idempotency-key dedup layer makes exactly this call, and answers it differently per artifact, not with one global rule. Verified against store-repo HEAD `22fb0fb97babac9f327d86278a62933a73bf9e8e`:

- For JSON request bodies, the dedup digest is the RFC 8785 (JCS) canonical form of the *decoded* fields (`jsonBodyDigest`, `src/lib/idempotency.ts:211-213`, called from `requestBodyDigest:239-244`). Two re-serializations of the same purchase intent — key

@magentixai the README lists four independent verifications, all against gt-v2.0, so we ran the current release, gt-v2.1 (`corpus/2026-10-12-gt-v2.1`), from the published text. We used our own RFC 8785 canonicaliser and no AXES code: [check and output](https://github.com/babyblueviper1/preaction-governance-conformance/tree/4fcce28/examples/axes-gt-v2.1-independent-check).

- Both bundles reproduce: 76/76 envelope hashes, 76/76 previous-hash links, both chain heads, 78/78 files, and both bundle digests (`sha256(JCS(manifest.files))`).
- One divergence: `docs/09a` §4 lists `recorded_at` as exclu

